Upstream-Name: quoth
Upstream-Contact: Samuel Ruairí Bullard <samuel.ruairi.bullard@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/abullard1/Quoth
Comment: The binary package bundles seven native components added at package
 time (not present in this source tree): whisper.cpp (libwhisper.so + ggml
 backends, MIT; it compiles in YaRN under MIT and Vulkan-Hpp, used under MIT),
 the trimmed Intel-NPU OpenVINO runtime (Apache-2.0, with oneTBB under
 Apache-2.0 and hwloc under BSD-3-Clause), Intel's prebuilt NPU driver stack
 (the user-mode driver, MIT; its compiler, Apache-2.0, compiling in LLVM and
 MLIR under Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, the legacy NCSA licence and
 BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Spencer and Unicode notices; the Level Zero
 loader, MIT), gtk4-layer-shell (MIT), ThorVG (MIT; it compiles in RapidJSON
 under MIT and code under the FreeType License and MPL-2.0), wl-clipboard's
 wl-copy and wl-paste (GPL-3.0-or-later), and ydotool's ydotool and ydotoold
 (AGPL-3.0-or-later). gtk4-layer-shell and wl-clipboard also compile in code
 generated from Wayland protocols under MIT and HPND-sell-variant terms.
 wl-clipboard, Copyright 2018-2026 Sergey Bugaev, and ydotool, Copyright
 2018-2022 Reimu NotMoe, are built unmodified from
 https://github.com/bugaevc/wl-clipboard and
 https://github.com/ReimuNotMoe/ydotool. packaging/pins.sh names each one's
 tag, commit or checksum; it is in quoth-VERSION.tar.gz on each release at
 https://github.com/abullard1/Quoth/releases, where quoth-deb-sources.tar.gz
 holds the unmodified source of wl-clipboard, ydotool and ThorVG at those
 commits, and the build distribution's wayland-protocols files that
 wl-clipboard generates code from, with that package's version. It also bundles
 the pure-Python Sentry SDK (MIT) privately under
 .../dist-packages/quoth/_vendor/, five Lucide icons (ISC), three adapted
 palettes (MIT upstream, GPL-3.0-or-later adaptation), and the Silero VAD model
 in whisper.cpp's GGML format (MIT). Each ships its own license text beside the
 bundled files or under /usr/share/licenses/quoth/.

